    passageB1: `<p>We all <strong>get older</strong>, even if we try to stop it. It's part of life. Some people use makeup or <strong>have surgery</strong> to look younger. They might <strong>dye their hair</strong> to hide grey hairs. But we can't stay young forever.</p>

<p><strong>Medical advances</strong> help people live longer. But it's important to have a good life, and everyone ages differently. Some older people are healthy and can <strong>take care of themselves</strong>. Others are not so lucky. They might need to live in special homes where they can get help.</p>

<p>One of the hardest things about getting old is that your mind might not be as <strong>sharp</strong>. Older people sometimes <strong>forget things</strong> that just happened. But they might remember things from a long time ago very well. Later, some people get <strong>dementia</strong>, like Alzheimer's disease. This disease gets worse over time.</p>

<p>But not all older people have these problems. Many <strong>senior citizens</strong> are still very smart and see retirement as a time to be free. If they have a good <strong>pension</strong>, they might have enough money to go on holidays and buy nice things. Because of this, businesses and the government <strong>respect</strong> older people and their money.</p>

<p>However, not everyone treats older people well. In some cultures, people <strong>respect their elders</strong> a lot. But in other places, people don't think old people are important and treat them badly. These people are <strong>ageist</strong>. They might think old people are <strong>frail</strong> and close to death. They should remember that they will be old one day too.</p>`,
    translationB1: `<p>Biz hammamiz <strong>qarayamiz</strong>, hatto buni to'xtatishga harakat qilsak ham. Bu hayotning bir qismi. Ba'zi odamlar yoshroq ko'rinish uchun pardoz vositalaridan foydalanadilar yoki <strong>operatsiya qildiradilar</strong>. Ular oq sochlarini yashirish uchun <strong>sochlarini bo'yashlari</strong> mumkin. Ammo biz abadiy yosh bo'lib qololmaymiz.</p>

<p><strong>Tibbiyotdagi yutuqlar</strong> odamlarning uzoqroq yashashiga yordam beradi. Ammo yaxshi hayot kechirish muhim va har kim har xil tarzda qaridi. Ba'zi keksa odamlar sog'lom va <strong>o'zlariga g'amxo'rlik qila oladilar</strong>. Boshqalarning omadi kelmaydi. Ularga yordam olishlari mumkin bo'lgan maxsus uylarda yashashlari kerak bo'lishi mumkin.</p>

<p>Qarishning eng qiyin narsalaridan biri shundaki, aqlingiz unchalik <strong>o'tkir</strong> bo'lmasligi mumkin. Keksa odamlar ba'zan yaqinda sodir bo'lgan <strong>narsalarni unutadilar</strong>. Ammo ular uzoq vaqtdan oldin bo'lgan narsalarni juda yaxshi eslashlari mumkin. Keyinchalik, ba'zi odamlar Altsgeymer kasalligi kabi <strong>demensiya</strong> bilan kasallanadilar. Bu kasallik vaqt o'tishi bilan yomonlashadi.</p>

<p>Ammo barcha keksa odamlarda bu muammolar bo'lmaydi. Ko'p <strong>pensionerlar</strong> hali ham juda aqlli va nafaqani erkin bo'lish vaqti deb bilishadi. Agar ularning yaxshi <strong>pensiyasi</strong> bo'lsa, ularda ta'tilga chiqish va chiroyli narsalarni sotib olish uchun etarli pul bo'lishi mumkin. Shu sababli, biznes va hukumat keksa odamlarni va ularning pullarini <strong>hurmat qiladi</strong>.</p>

<p>Biroq, hamma ham keksa odamlarga yaxshi munosabatda bo'lmaydi. Ba'zi madaniyatlarda odamlar <strong>kattalarini</strong> juda hurmat qiladilar. Ammo boshqa joylarda odamlar qariyalarni muhim deb hisoblamaydilar va ularga yomon munosabatda bo'lishadi. Bu odamlar <strong>yoshga nisbatan kamsituvchi</strong>. Ular qariyalarni <strong>zaif</strong> va o'limga yaqin deb o'ylashlari mumkin. Ular bir kun kelib o'zlari ham qarib qolishlarini unutmasliklari kerak.</p>`,
